    "result_text": "Full suite is green: **279 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the per-city owner cap on `POST /api/owners`, following the existing \"reject\" pattern in this OfficeFloor codebase.\n\n**New files:**\n- `RejectOwnerCityLimit.java` \u2014 pipeline step: counts existing owners whose city matches the new owner's city (case/whitespace-insensitive, via the existing `DuplicateMatching` helper) and throws `OwnerCityLimitException` when the count is already \u2265 8.\n- `OwnerCityLimitException.java` \u2014 checked exception (mirrors `DailyOwnerLimitException`).\n- `OwnerCityLimitExceptionHandler.java` \u2014 responds **400 Bad Request** with a `ProblemDetail`.\n- `...OwnerCityLimitException.yml` \u2014 escalation wiring for the handler.\n\n**Modified:**\n- `owners.POST.yml` \u2014 inserted a `rejectCityLimit` step right after `normalizeCity` (so the count uses the normalized city spelling) and before the existing reject steps.\n\nThe pre-existing `Cp14Tests` (8 owners in a city, then the 9th rejected with 400) now passes, and the daily-cap test `Cp13Tests` still passes since its owners use distinct cities.",
